ex:cqPrescriptionKinds a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:PrescriptionKind } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Twelve kinds, and the roster is the slice.s claim that one prescription vocabulary spans a recipe, a lab protocol, a CI build and a curriculum rather than each domain minting its own. The value of pinning it is negative: if a thirteenth kind can be added without a fight, the kinds have stopped being a closed classification of repeatable work and become a free-text label with extra steps. They are individuals, never subclasses, so a new domain is a new individual and never a new class (Principle 9)." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindAgentFlow , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindBusinessProcess , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindCiBuild , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindControlPlan , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindCurriculum , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindDataPipeline , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindIngestion , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindLabProtocol , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindOrganizationalGuide , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindRecipe , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindRepeatableGuide , ex:cqPrescriptionKindsRowprescriptionKindResearchPlan  .

