ex:cqSkipReasons a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:SkipReason } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A skipped step must say WHY, and the four reasons are not interchangeable: already-satisfied means the work was done elsewhere, not-applicable means it never applied, policy-excluded means a rule removed it, and operator-declined means a person refused it. Only the last two are decisions someone can be asked about, and an untyped skip erases that difference, which is precisely how a declined step later reads as an inapplicable one in a review." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipAlreadySatisfied , ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipNotApplicable , ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipOperatorDeclined , ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipPolicyExcluded  .

ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipAlreadySatisfied a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:SkipAlreadySatisfied ] .
ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipNotApplicable a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:SkipNotApplicable ] .
ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipOperatorDeclined a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:SkipOperatorDeclined ] .
ex:cqSkipReasonsRowSkipPolicyExcluded a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:SkipPolicyExcluded ] .

ex:cqRejectionKinds a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:RejectionKind } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A refinement that discards a candidate must record which of the four gates it failed, because each has a different remedy: a precondition can be established, a capability can be acquired, a resource can be waited for, and an approval can be sought. A single rejected flag makes all four look like the same dead end and hides the fact that three of them are actionable. The roster is pinned by IRI so that folding, say, capability and resource into one unavailable value fails here rather than silently halving the advice a planner can give." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedApproval , ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedCapability , ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedPrecondition , ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedResource  .

ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedApproval a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RejectedApproval ] .
ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedCapability a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RejectedCapability ] .
ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedPrecondition a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RejectedPrecondition ] .
ex:cqRejectionKindsRowRejectedResource a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RejectedResource ] .

ex:cqIntegrityFaults a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:IntegrityFault } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The four integrity faults name the ways a derived artifact can betray the inputs it claims to derive from: its content hash disagrees, it was built from the wrong generation of data, its identity does not match the record pointing at it, or it was rematerialized rather than restored. They are not severities of one fault; they have different repairs, and only the rematerialization case is ever benign. An untyped integrity error would put all four behind one alarm, which is how the benign one trains an operator to ignore the other three." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultContentIntegrity , ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultDataGeneration , ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultIdentityMismatch , ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultRematerialization  .

ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultContentIntegrity a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultContentIntegrity ] .
ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultDataGeneration a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultDataGeneration ] .
ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultIdentityMismatch a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultIdentityMismatch ] .
ex:cqIntegrityFaultsRowFaultRematerialization a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultRematerialization ] .

ex:cqIncompleteCauses a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:IncompleteCause } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "When a derivation stops short, the cause decides whether the result may be trusted at all: a step or page budget cut is a resource limit that a rerun can lift, a deadline is a wall-clock limit that a rerun may hit again, and a cancellation is a decision that a rerun would override. Reporting only that the run was incomplete leaves a reader unable to tell a recoverable truncation from a deliberate stop, and it is that ambiguity, not the truncation itself, that lets a cut roster pass for a closed one." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteCancellation , ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteDeadline , ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompletePageBudget , ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteStepBudget  .

ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteCancellation a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:IncompleteCancellation ] .
ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteDeadline a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:IncompleteDeadline ] .
ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompletePageBudget a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:IncompletePageBudget ] .
ex:cqIncompleteCausesRowIncompleteStepBudget a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:IncompleteStepBudget ] .

ex:cqApprovalBindingFaults a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:ApprovalBindingFault } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "An approval binds to one intent of one enactment inside one window under one operator policy, and the four faults are exactly the four ways that binding can be broken. They are kept apart because only one of them is an attack: a digest mismatch means the approved intent is not the dispatched one, which is approval laundering, whereas an expired window is ordinary staleness. A generic invalid approval would hide the laundering case among three innocuous ones." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultDifferentEnactment , ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultDigestMismatch , ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultExpiredWindow , ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultOperatorPolicyMismatch  .

ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultDifferentEnactment a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultDifferentEnactment ] .
ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultDigestMismatch a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultDigestMismatch ] .
ex:cqApprovalBindingFaultsRowFaultExpiredWindow a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FaultExpiredWindow ] .
