ex:cqReconciliationVerdicts a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:ReconciliationVerdict } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A reconciliation probe returns one of three verdicts, and the third is the point: still-unknown is a POSITIVE result, not a missing one. A two-valued committed/not-committed reading has nowhere to put the answer the provider actually gave, so it must guess, and the guess is what authorizes the blind retry the protocol exists to forbid. Pinning all three by IRI is what stops still-unknown being quietly re-read as not-committed the next time the roster is edited." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledCommitted , ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledNotCommitted , ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledStillUnknown  .

ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledCommitted a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ReconciledCommitted ] .
ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledNotCommitted a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ReconciledNotCommitted ] .
ex:cqReconciliationVerdictsRowReconciledStillUnknown a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ReconciledStillUnknown ] .

ex:cqRebuildReasons a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:RebuildReason } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "An incremental engine that gives up must say why it gave up, because the three reasons predict different futures: a changed fragment or rule set will recur every time that input changes, whereas a non-incremental retraction is a one-off. Reporting a bare full rebuild leaves a maintainer unable to tell a systematic cost from an occasional one, and it is the systematic one that is worth engineering away." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildFragmentChanged , ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildNonIncrementalRetraction , ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildRuleSetChanged  .

ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildFragmentChanged a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RebuildFragmentChanged ] .
ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildNonIncrementalRetraction a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RebuildNonIncrementalRetraction ] .
ex:cqRebuildReasonsRowRebuildRuleSetChanged a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:RebuildRuleSetChanged ] .

ex:cqDeliverySemantics a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:DeliverySemantics } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Three delivery semantics, recorded on the idempotency contract rather than assumed by the caller. The roster matters because at-most-once and at-least-once fail in opposite directions — one loses effects, the other duplicates them — and a system that does not write down which one a provider offers will pick the recovery strategy for the other. Exactly-once is included as a claim a provider may make, not as a default, which is what keeps it falsifiable." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryAtLeastOnce , ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryAtMostOnce , ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryExactlyOnce  .

ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryAtLeastOnce a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:DeliveryAtLeastOnce ] .
ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryAtMostOnce a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:DeliveryAtMostOnce ] .
ex:cqDeliverySemanticsRowDeliveryExactlyOnce a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:DeliveryExactlyOnce ] .

ex:cqContinuationKinds a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:ContinuationKind } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "When an enactment picks up again, exactly one of three things is happening: it resumes where it stopped, it repeats work it already did, or it continues under a revised prescription. These are not shades of restart — resume and repeat differ on whether committed effects are re-issued, and revise differs from both on whether the plan being followed is still the one that was approved. A single continued flag would let a repeat pass for a resume, which is the duplicate-effect bug stated in vocabulary form." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationRepeat , ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationResume , ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationRevise  .

ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationRepeat a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ContinuationRepeat ] .
ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationResume a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ContinuationResume ] .
ex:cqContinuationKindsRowContinuationRevise a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:ContinuationRevise ] .

ex:cqSearchFragments a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:SearchFragment } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Means-end refinement is undecidable in general, so the kernel names the three decidable fragments a search may declare itself inside — a totally ordered method set, an acyclic method graph, or a depth bound. The roster is what turns termination from a hope into a declared property: a search that names no fragment is claiming nothing, and a search that names one has made a checkable promise. Pinning the three by IRI stops a fourth being added without the termination argument that would justify it." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentAcyclicMethod , ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentBoundedDepth , ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentTotallyOrdered  .

ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentAcyclicMethod a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FragmentAcyclicMethod ] .
ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentBoundedDepth a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FragmentBoundedDepth ] .
ex:cqSearchFragmentsRowFragmentTotallyOrdered a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:FragmentTotallyOrdered ] .

ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditions a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a logic:UnsupportedFragmentCondition } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "When an engine refuses a fragment it must say which of three conditions it hit: a construct it does not implement, a method set it cannot order, or a rule set it cannot show terminating. The first is a gap in the engine and the other two are properties of the input, so routing all three to one unsupported message sends a user to fix their data when the engine is at fault, or the reverse." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedConstruct , ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedMethodSet , ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedNonTerminating  .

ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedConstruct a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:UnsupportedConstruct ] .
ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedMethodSet a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:UnsupportedMethodSet ] .
ex:cqUnsupportedFragmentConditionsRowUnsupportedNonTerminating a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:UnsupportedNonTerminating ] .

# --- Per-record carrier rosters ----------------------------------------------
#
# The eight questions below read each kernel record's DECLARED carrier set off
# rdfs:domain and pin it as (record, carrier) pairs. A record whose carrier set
# has quietly lost a member still validates, still renders, and still reads as
# complete — the omission is invisible to exactly the reader it misleads — so
# the pin is over pairs rather than over a count per record: a count survives a
# swap that drops one carrier and adds another, and the swap is the drift these
# questions exist to catch. The VALUES block is what scopes each question to one
# named subsystem instead of to every domained property in the merged canon.

ex:cqRecordCarriersShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "record" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "term" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriers a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> SELECT ?record ?term WHERE { VALUES ?record { logic:Enactment logic:TransitionJournal logic:JournalEntry logic:InputSnapshot logic:SnapshotDelta } ?term rdfs:domain ?record } ORDER BY ?record ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The five records that make an enactment auditable: the run itself, its journal and journal entries, the input snapshot it was launched over, and the delta that relates one snapshot generation to the next. The pin matters most on the journal entry, whose five carriers are the whole append-only argument — a previous head, a new head, a delta identity, an outcome tag and a link to the predecessor entry. Drop any one and the chain stops being verifiable while still looking like a log; drop the guard formula on the enactment and a version can be revised under a running enactment with nothing to say so." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqRecordCarriersShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactmentContextAssembly , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactmentInputSnapshot , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactmentJournal , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactmentState , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactsPrescriptionVersion , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowEnactmentenactedPrescriptionDigest , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowInputSnapshotsnapshotDigest , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowJournalEntryjournalPredecessor , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowJournalEntryjournalDeltaIdentity , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowJournalEntryjournalNewHead , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowJournalEntryjournalOutcomeTag , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowJournalEntryjournalPrevHead , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowSnapshotDeltadeltaAddition , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowSnapshotDeltadeltaSuppression , ex:cqEnactmentCoreCarriersRowTransitionJournaljournalHead  .

