ex:cqApprovalCarriers a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> SELECT ?record ?term WHERE { VALUES ?record { logic:ApprovalCommitment logic:Advisory logic:AuthorizationProof } ?term rdfs:domain ?record } ORDER BY ?record ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Approval, advice and proof are three different things and the carrier sets say so. A commitment carries the enactment and intent digest it binds to, the operator and policy that issued it, its validity window, its decision and the governing norm — seven carriers, and it is the intent digest that makes it an approval of a specific action rather than a general blessing. An advisory carries only what it is about, because advice authorizes nothing. An authorization proof carries what it establishes. A surface that gave the advisory an approval-shaped carrier set would be one edit away from laundering advice into authorization." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqRecordCarriersShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowAdvisoryadvisoryAbout , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalGoverningNorm , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalDecision , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalEnactment , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalIntentDigest , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalOperator , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalPolicy , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowApprovalCommitmentapprovalValidityWindow , ex:cqApprovalCarriersRowAuthorizationProofproofEstablishes  .

