ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigests a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term a owl:DatatypeProperty . FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?term), \"https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/checkpoint\")) } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A checkpoint is only restorable if the world it is restored into is the world it was taken from, and the seven component digests are what make that checkable: the data, the rule set, the slice set, the engine, the contract, the annotations and the fragment. The eighth entry is the composite descriptor hash they roll up into. Enumerating the components rather than shipping only the composite is the whole design — a single opaque hash tells a reader that something changed, and these tell them WHICH thing changed, which is the difference between a restore that can be repaired and one that can only be abandoned." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointAnnotationDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointContractDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointDataDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointDescriptorHash , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointEngineDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointFragmentDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointRulesDigest , ex:cqCheckpointDescriptorDigestsRowcheckpointSliceDigest  .

