ex:cqAttemptReferents a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> SELECT ?term WHERE { ?term rdfs:range logic:EffectAttempt } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Seven relations point back at an effect attempt, and that convergence is the protocol design rather than an accident of naming. An attempt is the only handle an external effect is ever known through, so the receipt that settles it, the unknown outcome that fails to, the probe that interrogates it, the impossibility that forecloses it, the retry that repeats it, the licence that permits the retry and the adjudication that resolves a contradiction about it all target the ATTEMPT and not the step or the enactment. Pin the set and a new recovery record cannot be added that hangs off the step instead, which is how an effect ends up with two recovery stories that never meet." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowadjudicatesAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowimpossibleOfAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowlicenceCoversAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowprobesAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowreceiptOfAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowretryOfAttempt , ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowunknownOfAttempt  .

ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowadjudicatesAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:adjudicatesAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowimpossibleOfAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:impossibleOfAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowlicenceCoversAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:licenceCoversAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowprobesAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:probesAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowreceiptOfAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:receiptOfAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowretryOfAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:retryOfAttempt ] .
ex:cqAttemptReferentsRowunknownOfAttempt a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:unknownOfAttempt ] .

ex:cqLogicFailureClasses a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> SELECT DISTINCT ?term WHERE { ?c gmeow:enforcesFailureClass ?term . FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?term), \"https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/\")) } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Every constraint in the slice declares the failure class it enforces, and this reads the seven classes back off those declarations rather than off a hand-kept list. That direction is the point: a class nobody enforces would silently drop out of this roster, and a constraint that enforced a class the slice never declared would silently add to it. Enactment integrity is the largest of the seven and covers the fencing, digest, licence and journal laws together, because they all fail the same way — a run whose record no longer describes what happened." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowEnactmentIntegrityViolation , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowIncompleteClosure , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowSectionObligationViolated , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowUncertifiedChase , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowUnentrenchedCounterfactual , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowUnwiredFlagshipScenario , ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowUnwitnessedRefutation  .

ex:cqLogicFailureClassesRowEnactmentIntegrityViolation a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:EnactmentIntegrityViolation ] .
