ex:cqLawReadPredicates a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQuery "PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> SELECT DISTINCT ?term WHERE { ?f logic:relation ?term . FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?term), \"https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/\")) } ORDER BY ?term" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The slice ships its laws as logic:Formula abstract syntax rather than as prose or as hand-written SHACL, and the consequence is that the predicates those laws READ are queryable. This question asks for them, and its value is the gap it exposes: a kernel predicate absent from this roster is carried by records and read by nobody, which is either a law that was never written or a field that never mattered. Pinning the set exactly turns both directions into failures — deleting a law silently shrinks it, and adding an atom over a predicate the kernel does not declare silently grows it. The filter keeps the answer to logic-owned predicates; laws that read a gmeow: or math: predicate are that slice.s question to ask." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqKernelRosterShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
